Results concerning the second experiment revealed that overall, MS subjects committed more collisions and infractions than their controls (MS-Collisions median: 3 range:3-5; Control-Collision median: 1 range: 1-3; MSInfractions median: 7 range:5-7; Control-Infractions median: 3 range: 2-5) and tend to drive slower (MS-Max Speed median: 65Km/h range: 59-84Km/h; Control-Max Speed median: 80 Km/h range: 75-91Km/h), see Fig.5. Interestingly, the two groups do not show significant differences in terms of mean Speed (MS-Mean Speed median:28 Km/h range: 2333Km/h; Control-Mean Speed median 28 Km/h range:28-29 Km/h).
