IV. CONCLUSION Altogether, these preliminary results highlight several important points: (i) all the participants, including people with MS were overall fascinated by the Virtual Reality and felt immersed inside the virtual world during the driving; (ii) all the subjects show similar mean and variability of the speed, suggesting that the simulator simulates a real driving, thus causing realistic behaviors; (iii) all three MS subjects were

